{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Wrapped","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrapped implements Equatable based on an identity based on the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"pointer to the Godot native object and also implements the Identifiable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"protocol using this pointer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrapped manages the lifecycle of these objects, and in the event that an","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object in the Godot world has been disposed, the handle in the Wrapped"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object will be cleared - you can detect this condition by calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"isValid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"on the object.","type":"text"}]},{"level":1,"text":"State Management","type":"heading","anchor":"State-Management"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrapped manages the lifecycle of these objects, and in the event that an","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"object in the Godot world has been disposed, the handle in the Wrapped","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object will be cleared - you can detect this condition by calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValid"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the object.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrapped subclasses come in two forms: straight bindings to the Godot","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"API which are used to expose capabilities to developers.   These objects, referred"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to as Framework types do not have any additional state associated in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When user subclass Wrapped, they might have state associated with them,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"so those objects are preserved and are not thrown away until they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"explicitly relinquished by both Godot and any references you might hold to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them.   These are known as User types.   Objects can be subclassed either"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to attach additional runtime information, or to override methods (we follow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the Godot conventions and the methods are prefixed with an underscore).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"text":"LifeCycle","anchor":"LifeCycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some special handling is done for different objects in the Godot hierarchy.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The way we now handle the lifecycle of Godot objects in Swift is the following:"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"If an object is not a RefCounted, we keep a strong reference to it, so that only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"a call to the appropriate free method can delete the object.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If an object is a RefCounted, we keep track of the reference()\/unreference() calls","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to it, and we keep a weak reference to it if there are no references to it in Godot,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise we keep a strong reference to it. This guarantees that the object can","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still be deleted when no reference to it exists anymore, while making sure that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtyped objects keep their state on the Swift side throughout the Godot object’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"lifetime. As the Swift wrapper also increases the reference count of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"RefCounted, this means that once a RefCounted is passed to the Swift side, that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Godot object will always be destroyed by the Swift wrapper eventually."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Type Registration","level":1,"anchor":"Type-Registration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any subclass ends up calling the Wrapped(StringName) constructor which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provides the name of the most-derived framework type, and this constructor","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"determines whether this is a Framework type or a user type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To register User types with the framework make sure you call the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"register<T: Object> (type: T.Type)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method like this:"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"register (type: MySpinningCube.self)"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you do not call this method, many of the overloads that Godot would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call you back on will not be invoked."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/wrapped"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Wrapped\/==(_:_:)"],"anchor":"Operators"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/d